# Conformance probe pack for `switch` (spec 0.20): an ASTERIX-like synthetic
# record, most significant bit first. Public. No external standard.
#
#   FSPEC        presence p fx: one octet, p.1 to p.7 then the FX bit
#   p.1          an extensible item: [y : 1][x : 6][fx], then [c1 : 7][fx]
#                y is the type bit, read inside the `if` and the chain
#   then by y, the same presence bits laid out twice:
#     0     p.2 z : 8     p.3 w : 16     p.4 qty : 8
#     1     p.2 c2 : 16   p.3 n : 8      (p.4 is named by no line of case 1)
#     else  p.2 val : 8                  (y absent: p.1 was 0)
#
# Presence bits count the selected case only: on decode a bit that is 1 and
# that no `if` of the lines read names is malformed-wire; on encode a key of
# a case not selected sets no bit and is not written.
format     conformance-kinds-record
version    0.20.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
layout     sequential
bit_order  msb
presence p fx
if p.1
  chain
    field  probe.y  1  uint
    field  probe.x  6  uint
    fx
    field  probe.c1  7  uint
    fx
  end
end
switch probe.y
  case 0
    if p.2
      field  probe.z  8  uint
    end
    if p.3
      field  probe.w  16  uint
    end
    if p.4
      field  probe.qty  8  uint
    end
  case 1
    if p.2
      field  probe.c2  16  uint
    end
    if p.3
      field  probe.n  8  uint
    end
  else
    if p.2
      field  probe.val  8  uint
    end
end
